{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1468209-exalts-and-excellencies","id":1468209,"title":"\"Exalts and Excellencies\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-17T18:53:36-08:00","id":1468209,"title":"\"Exalts and Excellencies\"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Recently, I found myself in possession of five things:</span></span><ul><li>A frustration with the plodding pace and difficulty-in-creating-challenges of Exalted 3e combat</li> <li>A reminder of how much I enjoy Mutants and Masterminds</li> <li>An urge to endlessly tinker with RPG mechanics</li> <li>An excess of free time</li> <li>Severe psychological damage</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Long story short, now I have a sixth thing: </span></span><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XQdumCoCDl2jCDTbuyp4xXiRBuv4ANDVwCSpanmVZEE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">an insanely long set of rules for making M&amp;M feel as much like Exalted as possible</a><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, Tahoma, Calibri, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">. So, uh... check it out if you're interested, I guess? I'd particularly like some feedback on how I dealt with non-Solar Exalt types, and for anything important in the original system/setting that I've missed.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T19:49:52-08:00","id":1468215,"title":"","cont